mass-link-315d9492.conceptual_definition:
The expression $M_N \sim 10^{10} - 10^{15} 	ext{ GeV}$ specifies the characteristic mass scale for a sterile, right-handed Majorana neutrino ($N$). In the Type I seesaw mechanism, the mass of the light, active neutrinos ($m_{
u}$) is generated through the relation $m_{
u} \approx  rac{m_D^2}{M_N}$, where $m_D$ is a Dirac mass term. This vast mass scale for $M_N$ is therefore required to suppress $m_{
u}$ to the observed sub-eV level, assuming $m_D$ is of a typical electroweak scale.
